{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/112932-i-m-mad-as-hell-and-i-m-not-going-to-take-it-anymore-alternate-solar-limit-rules","id":112932,"title":"I'm Mad As Hell, And I'm Not Going To Take It Anymore: Alternate Solar Limit rules.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-14T14:28:23-07:00","id":112932,"title":"I'm Mad As Hell, And I'm Not Going To Take It Anymore: Alternate Solar Limit rules.","content":"<i>You feel it too, don't you? That tug in your head, telling you that the world is </i>wrong.<i> We are virtuous people, you and I; we wouldn't have been chosen otherwise. But the world isn't, and it would be so </i>easy <i>to just go along with whatever is the nice, expected behaviour everyone wants us to use. But sometimes...<br /> <br /> The easy way isn't the best way, understand?</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Solar Limit</b></span></span><br /> The Lawgivers are a passionate bunch; they wouldn't have had the drive to get chosen in the first place otherwise. And the problem with passionate people is that sometimes, their passions get away from them. It is an undeniable fact.<br /> <br /> But it wasn't always so... poisonous. When the war that slew the Ancients happened, the Lawgivers struck one, two, a dozen plus one killing blows; in their last gasp, the Neverborn, those world-makers who were never meant to die <i>but were slain</i> spoke one last curse.<br /> <div align=\"center\">May your passion and strength destroy you. May you look back upon your works and <i>despair</i>.</div> And lo, that is how it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b><ul><li>Each Solar has a <i>Flawed Virtue</i>, a piece of their character that is perhaps too large for their human nature. A Flawed Virtue must be rated at 3 or higher, and may not be reduced below that point through <i>any</i> means.</li> <li>Upon choosing their Flawed Virtue, the Solar's player also selects a single broad emotion; this is their <i>Flawed Passion.</i></li> <li>Whenever a Solar encounters a situation where they would have to suppress their Flawed Virtue, they may choose to <i>not</i> suppress it, regain a Virtue channel for that Virtue, and then enter a more specific form of their <i>Flawed Passion</i> as an Emotion effect; while under the effects of this Emotion effect, actions opposed to the Emotion take a -3 internal penalty, actions unrelated to the emotion take a -1 internal penalty, and actions that resonate with that emotion have their Stunt ratings improved by one step. This Emotion effect ignores any immunity or defence against Emotion effects that the Solar might have, and lasts until it burns out (i.e., until it is dramatically appropriate.)</li> <li>Whenever an effect grants some benefit to a Solar while they are Limit Breaking, they instead gain that benefit while under the effects of their <i>Flawed Passion</i>.</li> </ul><br /> <hr />An example: Steve is going to play Killfuck Soulshitter, and reasons &quot;hey, he's a pretty cool guy; kills Raksha and doesn't afraid of anything, so I'l give him Valor as his Flawed Virtue, and he seems like an angry guy, so I think Anger sound like a pretty neat Flawed Passion.&quot;<br /> <br /> A few sessions down the line, Killfuck is called out by a group of young punks; he has the choice of letting it slide, suppressing Valor and spending 1wp, or snapping, grabbing another Valor channel, and getting an Emotion effect of &quot;Annoyed Rage&quot;. He can either swallow his rage, or let it all come out.<br /> <br /> <b>Some Conversions:</b><br /> <u>Berserk Anger:</u> Flawed Valor, Anger.<br /> <u>Heart of Tears:</u> Flawed Compassion, Sadness<br /> <u>Heart of Flint:</u> Flawed Conviction, Determination<br /> <u>Ascetic Drive:</u> Flawed Temperance, Joy<br /> <hr />So here's a first draft. Right now, it can't do stuff like Overindulgence where you overcompensate for an inflated virtue, but otherwise... it allows for people to make up new Limit Breaks when building their character with a few simple questions.<br /> <br /> 1. Which Virtue matches your character the most?<br /> 2. How do they feel when they have to go against that Virtue?<br /> <br /> Another neat feature: if you are using alternate Virtues or whatever, it works <i>exactly the same.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T10:39:34-07:00","id":113419,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I figured out how to do opposition!<ul><li>When a player chooses their Solar's <i>Flawed Virtue</i>, they may choose to have that Flaw's expression be <i>Inverted</i>. If they do so, they still select a <i>Flawed Passion</i>; whenever they would suppress their <i>Flawed Virtue</i>, they may choose to enter a more specific form of their <i>Flawed Passion</i> instead of paying the Willpower cost.</li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> Now we get:<br /> <br /> <b>Overindulgence:</b> Flawed Temperance (Inverted), Joy<br /> <b>Deliberate Cruelty:</b> Flawed Compassion (Inverted), Determination (or Joy)<br /> <br /> Ta da!<br /> <br /> I'm open to feedback, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:03:11-07:00","id":113661,"title":"","content":"Nice. You can really get whatever you want out of this, WITHOUT your solar absolutely always doing the exact same thing in the exact same way. Rather than always breaking in the same way, they break in different ways.<br /> <br /> I also notice that this cuts out a running limit track, which is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:50:36-07:00","id":113688,"title":"","content":"Eh, who needs a running Limit track? That thing had a multitude of issues.<br /> <br /> That does add the issue that certain spells and charms have gaining Limit as a cost; I'd say that, for Solars at least, such costs are paid by you immediately needing to suppress that Virtue or enter a Flawed Passion.<br /> <br /> Now, from what I understand of the rest of the Exalted, their Limit works as follows:<br /> <b>Lunars:</b> Works like Solars, but they build up Permanent Limit that sends them Chimera. I can do something with this.<br /> <b>Dragon Blooded:</b> Work like Solars, but their Limit Breaks are aligned to their Aspects... Not sure what to do with them here.<br /> <b>Sidereals:</b> They make poor decisions and get Limit faster in groups. I like Revlid's alternate system (you know, randomly generated prophecy? Anyone save that?), adjusted to work with a not-ten-point-scale.<br /> <b>Abyssals:</b> Resonance... ew. Best I can come up with is something that gives them an incentive to hurt things (Stunt bonus if you include someone's death as a result of your action? That seems about right for part of it.)<br /> <b>Infernals:</b> Acts of Villainy are part of Torment, obviously; you'd have to make them more nuanced, but it still goes Affirming Action -&gt; OH LORDY I'M BROKEN. Urge can be rolled up into this.<br /> <b>Alchemicals:</b> Are perfect. No one is allowed to argue. Clarity actually works for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:16:15-07:00","id":113714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/112932-i-m-mad-as-hell-and-i-m-not-going-to-take-it-anymore-alternate-solar-limit-rules?p=113688#post113688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Alchemicals:</b> Are perfect. No one is allowed to argue. Clarity actually works for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not just make a Clarit-Alike for Virtues for Solars, wherein they take penalties for not seeing Everything through one of the four lenses of understanding?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:36:31-07:00","id":113729,"title":"","content":"Because as far as I see it, Clarity serves an entirely different function to Limit.<br /> <br /> Clarity is a measurement of how far you have drifted away from humanity, and towards being a MACHINE MAN. Limit is more about a &quot;perfect&quot; being getting stressed out when the world doesn't meet your standards.<br /> <br /> Clarity builds up slow; you gradually forget the feel of wind across your face as your mind shifts to match the inexorable patterns of a machine. Heck, I can see someone generate a lot of Clarity without even noticing, and then shrugging, because Clarity is not necessarily a <i>bad</i> thing. The fact that it slides up and down so easily fits with the modular nature of the Alchemicals as well.<br /> <br /> Limit, on the other hand, is emotional overflow; part of it is the fact that Solars are larger than life, so their emotions are similarly so. The 10-point scale would work if it was a stress thing for all of them, but I really believe Solar Limit should be more about temptation to have things go their way. In other words, they are tantrums, turned to 11.<br /> <br /> I could see a Clarity-a-like for <i>Terrestrials</i>, though, representing them getting closer to their Elemental counterparts. I could see one for Lunars, showing the madness of their chaos-broken souls.<br /> <br /> But not Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T19:14:10-07:00","id":113751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/112932-i-m-mad-as-hell-and-i-m-not-going-to-take-it-anymore-alternate-solar-limit-rules?p=113688#post113688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lunars:</b> Works like Solars, but they build up Permanent Limit that sends them Chimera. I can do something with this.<br /> <b>Sidereals:</b> They make poor decisions and get Limit faster in groups. I like Revlid's alternate system (you know, randomly generated prophecy? Anyone save that?), adjusted to work with a not-ten-point-scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Permanent limit is for casteless lunars only, a fact I enjoy because I've seen some good casteless homebrew that interacts with it interestingly.<br /> The alternative sidereal limit thing is indeed a fun one, though as with the general consciousness of the Exalted fanbase it likes to destroy Gem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:32:51-07:00","id":113778,"title":"","content":"Oh, right. Still, something can be done with it.<br /> <br /> And destroying Gem? That's only there because, well, it's an in joke. Gotta have those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}